---
import { domainWallSurface } from '../../../data/part06/ch28DiracModels.mjs';
const initialBulkMass = -1;
const vacuumMass = 2;
const initialSurfaceMass = 0;
const initial = domainWallSurface(initialBulkMass, vacuumMass, 1, initialSurfaceMass);
---

<figure class="chapter-visual surface-domain-wall" data-surface-domain-wall>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：Dirac mass domain wall、surface cone 与 time-reversal-breaking gap</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: Dirac-mass domain wall, surface cone, and a time-reversal-breaking gap</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls">
    <label>
      <span>bulk Dirac mass m<sub>bulk</sub></span>
      <input type="range" min="-2" max="2" step="0.05" value={initialBulkMass} data-dw-bulk />
      <output data-dw-bulk-out>{initialBulkMass.toFixed(2)}</output>
    </label>
    <label>
      <span>surface TR-breaking mass m<sub>s</sub></span>
      <input type="range" min="0" max="0.8" step="0.02" value={initialSurfaceMass} data-dw-surface />
      <output data-dw-surface-out>{initialSurfaceMass.toFixed(2)}</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 370" role="img" aria-labelledby="dw-title dw-desc">
    <title id="dw-title">Mass-domain-wall construction for a topological-insulator surface</title>
    <desc id="dw-desc">The left panel shows a bulk mass joined to a positive vacuum mass. The right panel shows a surface Dirac cone that gaps when a time-reversal-breaking surface mass is introduced.</desc>

    <g aria-label="mass profile">
      <line x1="60" y1="185" x2="355" y2="185" class="dw-axis" />
      <line x1="205" y1="45" x2="205" y2="320" class="dw-interface" />
      <path d="M70 240 L195 240 L215 85 L345 85" class="dw-mass-profile" data-dw-profile />
      <text x="92" y="62">crystal</text><text x="265" y="62">vacuum/reference</text>
      <text x="78" y="270" data-dw-left-label>m_bulk = −1.00</text>
      <text x="245" y="115">m_vac = +2.00</text>
      <text x="170" y="345">surface coordinate z</text>
      <circle cx="205" cy="185" r="9" class="dw-mode" data-dw-mode />
      <text x="220" y="205" data-dw-mode-label>localized interface mode</text>
    </g>

    <g aria-label="surface Dirac spectrum">
      <line x1="430" y1="185" x2="720" y2="185" class="dw-axis" />
      <line x1="575" y1="45" x2="575" y2="320" class="dw-axis" />
      <path d="M450 305 L575 185 L700 65" class="dw-band" data-dw-upper />
      <path d="M450 65 L575 185 L700 305" class="dw-band dw-band--second" data-dw-lower />
      <line x1="552" y1="185" x2="598" y2="185" class="dw-gap" data-dw-gap-marker />
      <text x="438" y="342">surface momentum k∥</text>
      <text x="596" y="65">E+</text><text x="596" y="305">E−</text>
      <text x="510" y="32">surface spectrum</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span data-dw-sign>bulk/vacuum sign change = yes</span>
    <span data-dw-localization>localization length ξ = {initial.localizationLength.toFixed(2)}</span>
    <span data-dw-gap>surface gap = {initial.surfaceGap.toFixed(2)}</span>
    <strong data-dw-status>A mass sign change supports one interface Dirac cone in the declared continuum model.</strong>
  </div>

  <p class="chapter-visual__fallback"><strong>静态回退 | Static fallback:</strong> 初始 <code>m_bulk=-1</code> 与 <code>m_vac=+2</code> 异号，连续 Dirac model 产生局域 interface mode；<code>m_s=0</code> 时表面 cone 无隙。该图不替代 lattice regularization、full-BZ invariant 或 slab calculation。</p>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong>三维 continuum Dirac Hamiltonian 的质量 <code>m(z)</code> 在晶体与 vacuum reference 之间改变符号。Jackiw–Rebbi-type domain-wall solution 给出表面 Hamiltonian <code>Hsurf=v(kx sy−ky sx)+ms sz</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> the mass <code>m(z)</code> of a three-dimensional continuum Dirac Hamiltonian changes sign between the crystal and a vacuum reference. A Jackiw–Rebbi-type domain-wall solution yields <code>Hsurf=v(kx sy−ky sx)+ms sz</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>两侧质量异号时 interface mode 存在，粗略 localization length 为 <code>v/min(|mbulk|,|mvac|)</code>；同号时该特定 domain-wall mechanism 不产生 mode。<code>ms=0</code> 时 cone 无隙，<code>ms≠0</code> 时 gap 为 <code>2|ms|</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> opposite mass signs support an interface mode with the rough localization length <code>v/min(|mbulk|,|mvac|)</code>. Equal signs do not support this domain-wall mechanism. The cone is gapless for <code>ms=0</code> and has gap <code>2|ms|</code> for <code>ms≠0</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>质量符号是低能 basis 与 regularization 相关的代表。真实 strong index 需要完整 lattice occupied manifold。表面 mass 可由磁性、有限厚度 hybridization 或 interactions 产生，但这些机制的对称性和 thickness dependence 必须分别检查。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the mass sign is a representative tied to a low-energy basis and regularization. A real strong index requires the complete lattice occupied manifold. A surface gap may arise from magnetism, finite-thickness hybridization, or interactions, whose symmetry and thickness dependence must be checked separately.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import { domainWallSurface } from '../../../data/part06/ch28DiracModels.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-surface-domain-wall]').forEach((root) => {
    const bulkInput = root.querySelector('[data-dw-bulk]');
    const surfaceInput = root.querySelector('[data-dw-surface]');
    if (!(bulkInput instanceof HTMLInputElement) || !(surfaceInput instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;
    const setText = (selector, value) => {
      const element = root.querySelector(selector);
      if (element) element.textContent = value;
    };
    const update = () => {
      const bulkMass = Number(bulkInput.value);
      const surfaceMass = Number(surfaceInput.value);
      const result = domainWallSurface(bulkMass, 2, 1, surfaceMass);
      setText('[data-dw-bulk-out]', bulkMass.toFixed(2));
      setText('[data-dw-surface-out]', surfaceMass.toFixed(2));
      setText('[data-dw-left-label]', `m_bulk = ${bulkMass >= 0 ? '+' : '−'}${Math.abs(bulkMass).toFixed(2)}`);
      setText('[data-dw-sign]', `bulk/vacuum sign change = ${result.signChange ? 'yes' : 'no'}`);
      setText('[data-dw-localization]', Number.isFinite(result.localizationLength)
        ? `localization length ξ = ${result.localizationLength.toFixed(2)}`
        : 'localization length ξ = ∞ / no bound mode');
      setText('[data-dw-gap]', result.surfaceGap === null ? 'surface gap = not applicable' : `surface gap = ${result.surfaceGap.toFixed(2)}`);
      const mode = root.querySelector('[data-dw-mode]');
      mode?.classList.toggle('dw-mode--absent', !result.signChange);
      setText('[data-dw-mode-label]', result.signChange ? 'localized interface mode' : 'no domain-wall mode');
      const gapMarker = root.querySelector('[data-dw-gap-marker]');
      if (gapMarker instanceof SVGLineElement) {
        const half = 8 + 40 * surfaceMass;
        gapMarker.setAttribute('x1', String(575 - half));
        gapMarker.setAttribute('x2', String(575 + half));
        gapMarker.classList.toggle('dw-gap--open', result.signChange && surfaceMass > 0);
      }
      const status = !result.signChange
        ? 'No mass sign change: this continuum interface has no protected domain-wall cone.'
        : surfaceMass > 0
          ? 'Interface mode retained, but a declared time-reversal-breaking surface mass opens a gap.'
          : 'A mass sign change supports one interface Dirac cone in the declared continuum model.';
      setText('[data-dw-status]', status);
    };
    [bulkInput, surfaceInput].forEach((input) => input.addEventListener('input', update));
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .surface-domain-wall svg { width: 100%; max-height: 28rem; }
  .surface-domain-wall text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .dw-axis { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .dw-interface { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4); stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }
  .dw-mass-profile { fill: none; stroke: var(--sl-color-text-accent); stroke-width: 4; }
  .dw-mode { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .dw-mode--absent { fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4); opacity: 0.45; }
  .dw-band { fill: none; stroke: var(--sl-color-text-accent); stroke-width: 3; }
  .dw-band--second { stroke: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .dw-gap { stroke: transparent; stroke-width: 8; }
  .dw-gap--open { stroke: var(--sl-color-red-high, #b42318); }
</style>
